A. Prim’s Algorithm
Start.
Initialize the weighted graph using an adjacency matrix.
Mark all vertices as unvisited.
Select vertex 0 as the starting vertex and mark it as visited.
Initialize the total cost to 0.
Find the minimum-weight edge connecting a visited vertex to an unvisited vertex.
Select that edge and add it to the Minimum Spanning Tree (MST).
Mark the newly connected vertex as visited.
Add the selected edge's weight to the total cost.
