B. Kruskal’s Algorithm
Start.
Initialize the weighted graph and store all edges with their weights.
Sort all edges in ascending order of their weights.
Initialize each vertex as a separate set.
Select the edge with the minimum weight.
Find the sets of the two vertices connected by the selected edge.
If both vertices belong to different sets, add the edge to the MST and combine their sets.
If both vertices belong to the same set, discard the edge to avoid forming a cycle.
Add the selected edge's weight to the total cost.
Repeat Steps 5–9 until � edges are selected.
Display the selected edges and the total cost.
Stop.
